  "verdict": "Dropping the relation from the query is the win: +0.025 AUPRC over V3ens (paired bootstrap p=0.003) and +0.028 held-out F1 (better on 96% of 1000 splits), at identical CPU cost. Entity markers alone are null. No encoder swap beat BiomedBERT-base. McNemar vs the deployed V1 on its 141 rows never clears 3.84 (best p=0.17), because 5 of the 8 remaining errors are rows whose TRAINING label is full-triple - they need the species-level relabel, not an architecture change.",
