  "cpu_throughput_note": "On a quiet box with dynamic padding all three 110M input formats run within 3% of each other (39-40 pairs/s), so the input format is throughput-neutral. Two real speed findings: (1) dynamic padding instead of padding every example to max_length raises 110M throughput from the recorded 24.2 to 39.4 pairs/s with numerically identical outputs (max logit diff 3.6e-7); (2) MiniLMv2-L6 (22.7M) reaches 217.8 pairs/s, 5.5x, but costs 0.041 AUPRC.",
